---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SELF_HOST_GUIDE_PATH } from "../site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · ALMA"
  description="ALMA AI prepares drafts for review."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Header />
    <main id="main" class="privacy-copy">
      <h1>About ALMA</h1>
      <p>
        ALMA AI prepares drafts for review. Bots can use a browser and a shell, remember the work around a
        job, run routines on a schedule, and ask for approval when they reach a boundary. It is designed for
        practical operational work rather than one-off chat.
      </p>
      <h2>Why we are building it</h2>
      <p>
        Useful agents should be understandable and controllable by the people who run them. ALMA keeps
        routines in readable Markdown, supports multiple model providers, records actions in an audit log, and
        lets operators keep model keys, browser sessions, and deployment infrastructure under their own
        control. The same bots and routines work across the web, desktop, and mobile clients.
      </p>
      <h2>Open by default</h2>
      <p>
        ALMA AI is maintained by ALMA INTELIGENCIA, S.R.L. and released under the Apache-2.0 license. To run ALMA on your own
        infrastructure, start with the <a href={SELF_HOST_GUIDE_PATH}>self-hosting guide</a>. For product or account help,
        email <a href="mailto:hello@rakazo.com">hello@rakazo.com</a>.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
